1.1.text:
Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:

1. Regional Government is the Government of Sumenep Regency; 2. Regent is the Regent of Sumenep;
3. Regional Apparatus is an organization/institution within the Regional Government responsible to the Regional Head in the context of government administration consisting of the Regional Secretariat, Regional Agencies and Regional Technical Institutions, Districts and Civil Service Police Units according to regional needs;
4. Implementation is a form of executing protection for women and children victims of violence;
5. Child is a person under 18 years of age, including those in the womb;
6. Violence is any act against the law that results in or may result in suffering or distress, whether physical, sexual, economic, social, or psychological to the victim;
7. Violence against Women is any action that results in or may result in suffering or distress to women physically, sexually, economically, socially, psychologically, including threats of certain actions, coercion or deprivation of freedom, whether occurring in public or private life;
8. Violence against children is any action that results in or may result in discrimination, exploitation, whether economic or sexual, neglect, cruelty, abuse, injustice and other mistreatment;

9.

Physical Violence is any act that causes pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, fainting and/or causes death;

10. Sexual Violence is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual intercourse, forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner, forced sexual intercourse with others for commercial and/or certain purposes;

11. Economic Violence is any act that neglects family members in the form of not providing proper livelihood, care or maintenance;

12. Psychological Violence is any act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or severe psychological suffering to a person;

13. Victim is a woman and child who experiences suffering and/or distress either directly or indirectly as a result of violence;

14. Protection of Women is all activities aimed at providing security carried out by the police, prosecutors, courts, social institutions, or other parties who know or hear that violence against women will or has occurred; 15. Child Protection is all activities to guarantee and protect children and their rights so that they can live, grow, develop and participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and receive protection from violence and discrimination; 16. Integrated Service Center for the Protection of Women and Children, hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A, is a service center that has the task and function of coordinating with related institutions in formulating technical policies and implementing prevention and eradication as well as elimination of acts of violence against children and women, implementing prevention and eradication of acts of violence against women and children in accordance with applicable laws and regulations as well as implementing policies and preventing problems in the field;

17. Community Social Institution is a Non-Governmental Organization (NGO) and/or other community organizations; 18. Population is Indonesian citizens and foreigners who enter legally and reside in the territory of Indonesia.

Implementation

A

A

GOVERNMENT OF SUMENEP REGENCY

REGIONAL REGULATION OF SUMENEP REGENCY NUMBER: 7 OF 2011 CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND

CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

Considering

REGENT OF SUMENEP

a. that the number of violence against women and children in Sumenep Regency is still high while services and protection for women and children in Sumenep Regency have not been carried out optimally;

b. that in the framework of implementing regional autonomy, the regulation and service to the community, especially for women and children victims of violence, is a duty and function of the regency government because violence against women and children is a violation of Human Rights; that based on the considerations referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence in the Regional Regulation of Sumenep Regency.

C.

In view of: 1. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3277); 2. Law Number 5 of 1998 concerning Ratification of the Convention Against Torture and Other Cruel, Inhuman or Degrading Treatment or Punishment (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1998 Number 164, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3783);

3. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3886);

4. Law Number 1 of 2000 concerning ILO Convention number 182 concerning the Prohibition and Immediate Action for the Elimination of the Worst Forms of Child Labor (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2001 Number 30, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 3941);

5. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4235);

6. Law Number 10 of 2004 concerning Formulation of Legislation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 53, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4389);

7. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4419);

8. Law Number 32 of 2004 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 125, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4437), as amended for the second time by Law Number 12 of 2008 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2008 Number 59, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4844);

9. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4720);

10. Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4593);

11. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation in Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

12. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs Between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette Number 4737);

13. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2006 concerning

Forms and Types of Regional Legal Products;

14. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 16 of 2006 concerning

Procedures and Formulation of Regional Legal Products;

15. Decree of the Minister of Home Affairs and Regional Autonomy Number 5

of 2001 concerning Prevention of Child Labor;

16. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) for integrated services for women and children victims of violence.

17. Regional Regulation of East Java Province Number 9 of 2005 concerning Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of East Java Province of 2005 Number 4 Series E);

18. Regional Regulation of Sumenep Regency number 4 of 2003 concerning Community Participation in Government and Development

With Mutual Approval

REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF SUMENEP

REGENCY and

REGENT OF SUMENEP

